in the Vienna talks Iran is negotiating  with six international powers the five  permanent members of the UN Security  Council and Germany or in short the p5  plus one they fear that Iran is trying  to develop nuclear weapons and in the  eyes of the p5 plus one that could pose  a major threat to world peace one focus  of discussions is nuclear enrichment for  an atomic bomb Iran would need highly  enriched uranium the International  powers want to limit in Richmond to 3.5  % enough for fuel for nuclear power  plants Iran in recent years managed to  enrich uranium to about twenty percent  that set off alarm bells for the p5 plus  one because it's a huge step towards  building nuclear weapons they are  demanding more international checks on  how many centrifuges Iran has available  for enrichment and on Iran's other  nuclear sites for the Iranians that's  going too far Tehran insists it's not  trying to develop atomic weapons and  wants only to harness nuclear power for  energy and medical purposes it's asking  for the international economic sanctions  to be eased they include a ban on  imports of Iranian oil to the European  Union one way forward could be a  combination of fewer sanctions and more  international inspections finding the  right balance could end the deadlock
 

